# <%= current_page.data.title %>

## Background

Default tags on AWS providers ensure that resources receive a consistent set of tags, even when tags are not specified on each resource.

The `business-unit` tag is used across the organisation for cost allocation and reporting.

Default tags must be configured for all Modernisation Platform accounts, including member accounts.

## How to Add Default Tags

To add default tags to AWS providers, you can use the following Terraform code:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "eu-west-2"

  default_tags {
    tags = local.tags
  }
}
```

Add the `default_tags` block to each provider that creates resources. The current Modernisation Platform templates already include this configuration.

## Important Note on Modules

Default tags apply to resources managed by the configured provider that support tagging. Modules inherit the caller's provider configuration unless they use a different provider configuration.

### Recommendation

Check the Terraform plan to confirm that the expected values appear in `tags_all`. Continue to pass a module's `tags` input where the module requires it or uses those values for its own logic.
